# .dockerignore -- repository-root context (this is the context the grader uses)
#
# Canonical copy: minivec/tools/scaffold/dockerignore.root
# `bash tools/ci.sh --sync` installs this file as <repo-root>/.dockerignore.
#
# The grader builds the image from the repository root, where our source lives
# in minivec/. The rest of this repository (seekdb tree, CI, docs, evidence)
# must never enter the build context: it is hundreds of megabytes and would slow
# the build without being used.
#
# Whitelist, so the context is exactly: minivec/Makefile + minivec/src/**.
# The Dockerfile accepts both layouts; this file is what keeps the root context
# small. Any new build input directory under minivec/ needs a rule here --
# `python3 tools/lint_packaging.py --repo <repo-root>` fails if one is missing.
*
!minivec
!minivec/Makefile
!minivec/src
!minivec/src/**

# never ship: VCS, tests, tooling, docs, agent evidence, built artifacts
.git
.git/**
.github
.github/**
minivec/.git
minivec/tests
minivec/tools
minivec/docs
minivec/agent
agent
agent/**
minivec/minivec
*.o
*.a
*.so
**/data
**/__pycache__
